la, and other GTM tools. Stay on top of accounts, complete follow-ups, and do deep research. cite49†pic.twitter.com/lgVfqrDbid†t.co L68: >\nL69: > — Grok Bot (@bot) cite50†September 10, 2026†x.com L70: “Grok Bot is now more powerful for sales teams,” the account wrote, pointing to those CRM and go-to-market hooks rather than a generic chatbot pitch. In a follow-up in the same thread, the company said it is also sharing its own sales team’s Bots as installable templates, each packed with context, connectors, and routines so a new sales agent is not starting from a blank chat.\nL71: > We’re also sharing our own sales team’s Bots as templates you can install.\nL72: >\nL73: > Each one comes with context, connectors, and routines to get you started.cite51†https://t.co/QFMn6B6LqX†t.co L74: >\nL75: > — Grok Bot (@bot) cite52†September 10, 2026†x.com L76: Musk quoted the announcement on September 11 with a blunt endorsement: “Grok @Bot is great for sales teams!” That keeps the product story on the same stack Tesla North has been tracking through the recent cite53†inline drafts and usage bump and the upcoming cite54†Grok Bot Galaxy sessions in San Francisco, which already carve out Sales, Sales Engineering, and SDR blocks for September 16.\nL77: > Grok cite55†@Bot†x.com is great for sales teams! cite56†https://t.co/JAL4H0QbNw†t.co L78: >\nL79: > — Elon Musk (@elonmusk) cite57†September 11, 2026†x.com L80: \nL81: The sales push is about putting agent work inside the tools reps already live in, instead of bouncing between a separate AI tab and the CRM. Named connectors for Salesforce and HubSpot matter more than another vague “AI for sales” slogan, and shipping internal sales-team Bots as templates suggests xAI is productizing how its own GTM org actually uses the stack.\nL82: Galaxy still runs September 15–17 at The Howard in San Francisco with a parallel livestream, so the CRM hooks land as homework you can try before the classroom sessions. Tesla North will watch whether more GTM connectors or published sales templates follow this first list.\nL83: \nL84: Want to see more of our stories on Google?\nL85: cite58†P.S. — Buying a new Tesla? Click here to save $1,000 USD, while supporting independent news.†ts.la L86: Help support us by cite59†shopping on Amazon here†amzn.to .\nL87: Links in this post are affiliate links, so we earn a tiny commission at no charge to you. Thanks for supporting independent media!\nL88: \nL89: Subscribe\nL90: \nL91: cite60†Image: guest†secure.gravatar.com L92: \nL93: Label\nL94: \nL95: [Button: {}] [Button: [+]]\nL96: \nL97: [Input]\nL98: \nL99: [Input: Name*] Name*\nL100: \nL101: [Input: Email*] Email*\nL102: \nL103: [Input: Website] Website\nL104: \nL105: [Input] [Input]\nL106: \nL107: [Input] [Input]\nL108: cite61†Image: guest†secure.gravatar.com L109: \nL110: Label\nL111: \nL112: [Button: {}] [Button: [+]]\nL113: \nL114: [Input]\nL115: \nL116: [Input: Name*] Name*\nL117: \nL118: [Input: Email*] Email*\nL119: \nL120: [Input: Website] Website\nL121: \nL122: [Input] [Input]\nL123: \nL124: [Input] [Input]\nL125: \nL126: 0 Comments\nL127: \nL128: Oldest\nL129: \nL130: Newest Most Voted\nL131: ## Other articles in the category: News\nL132: \nL133: cite62†SpaceX Details Starship Flight 14 First Orbit and 26 Starlink V3s L134: [caption id=\"attachment_72749\" align=\"aligncenter\" width=\"1024\"] Starship Flight 14 mission art. Credit: SpaceX[/caption] SpaceX has published the official Starship Flight 14 mission page, targeting a NET Tuesday, September 22, 2026, liftoff from Starbase pending regulatory approval, with a 75-minute window that opens at 7:15 a.m. Central Time. The company frames the flight as Starship’s first planned mission...\nL135: \nL136: cite47†Alex Diaz L137: \nL138: 3 hours ago\nL139: cite63†Tesla Accordion Supercharger: 16 Stalls Per Truck, 20% Cheaper L140: \nL141: Tesla Charging quietly introduced its first Accordion Supercharger on September 1